HigherCIOperators -- "Higher CI operators on a resolution over a complete intersection"
***************************************************************************************

Description
===========

The "higher CI operators" complete the structure of the ordinary CI operators
on (sometimes called "Eisenbud operators") on a resolution over a complete
intersection in the same sense that the "higher homotopies" complete the
structure of homotopies on with respect to a sequence of elements. Details will
appear in a preprint in preparation by Burke, Eisenbud and Schreyer.

The higher CI operators are constructed by the routine higherCIOperators.

Just as a system of higher homotopies for a regular sequence f_1..f_c on a
resolution over a ring S allow  one to construct the Shamash resolution over R
= S/(f_1..f_c), the higher CI operators are involved in a sort of dual
construction: from a resolution F over R, lifted to a sequence of maps A over
S, and lifted higher CI operators on A\otimes L, where L is the Koszul complex
on f, one can construct a nonminimal resolution AL over S using the routine
ciOperatorResolution.



