trueKoszul -- "Makes Koszul complex, with bases sorted in lex"
**************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        K = trueKoszul ff
  * Inputs:
      * ff, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, Matrix with the elements on
        which to build the Koszul complex
  * Outputs:
      * K, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, 

Description
===========

The usual Koszul command produces a complex with the basis sorted in revlex.
The sort in lex matches the sort of the monomials in the exterior algebra.

+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/101[a,b,c,d]                                |
|                                                        |
|o1 = S                                                  |
|                                                        |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                     |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : ff = matrix{{a,b,c,d}}                             |
|                                                        |
|o2 = | a b c d |                                        |
|                                                        |
|             1      4                                   |
|o2 : Matrix S  <-- S                                    |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : (koszulComplex ff).dd_2                            |
|                                                        |
|o3 = {1} | -b -c 0  -d 0  0  |                          |
|     {1} | a  0  -c 0  -d 0  |                          |
|     {1} | 0  a  b  0  0  -d |                          |
|     {1} | 0  0  0  a  b  c  |                          |
|                                                        |
|             4      6                                   |
|o3 : Matrix S  <-- S                                    |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : (trueKoszul ff).dd_2                               |
|                                                        |
|o4 = {1} | -b -c -d 0  0  0  |                          |
|     {1} | a  0  0  -c -d 0  |                          |
|     {1} | 0  a  0  b  0  -d |                          |
|     {1} | 0  0  a  0  b  c  |                          |
|                                                        |
|             4      6                                   |
|o4 : Matrix S  <-- S                                    |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : basis(2,(ZZ/101[a,b,c,d, SkewCommutative => true]))|
|                                                        |
|o5 = | ab ac ad bc bd cd |                              |
|                                                        |
|              ZZ       1       ZZ       6               |
|o5 : Matrix (---[a..d])  <-- (---[a..d])                |
|             101              101                       |
+--------------------------------------------------------+

